  "reasoning": "The product is a 1,2,3,4-tetrahydrocyclopenta[c]pyrrole derivative featuring a cyano-substituted saturated five-membered ring fused to an indole core. This bicyclic architecture is characteristic of a Diels-Alder [4+2] cycloaddition. Retrosynthetically, disconnecting the newly formed sigma bonds of the aliphatic ring reveals indole acting as the diene (across its C2-C3 bond) and acrylonitrile acting as the electron-deficient dienophile. The forward reaction cleanly constructs the fused cyclopentane ring while preserving the indole heterocycle, placing the cyano group at the expected position on the new ring.",
  "final_answer": "c1ccc2[nH]c(c2c1).C=CC#N"
}

